  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a string `s` which is composed of lowercase or uppercase letters, output the length of the **longest palindrome** that can be built with those letters.\n\nLetters are **case sensitive**, for example, `\"Aa\"` is not considered a palindrome.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"abccccdd\"\nOutput: 7\nExplanation: One longest palindrome that can be built is \"dccaccd\", whose length is 7.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"a\"\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: The longest palindrome that can be built is \"a\", whose length is 1.\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 2000`\n* `s` is composed of lowercase **and/or** uppercase English letters only.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
